+# Local music generation
+
+## When this is loaded
+
+The user chose to generate background music. It runs on the YuE2 model on the user's own server. `$MUSIC_API` and `$STT_API` are already set; there are no keys. The `yue2-song` skill describes the model in more depth.
+
+YuE2 is a song model. For an instrumental bed, the lyrics file holds only section labels and the style string asks for no vocals.
+
+## `generate.sh` template
+
+Write both files to `audio/originals/music/<slug>/`. `lyrics.txt`:
+
+```
+[Intro: instrumental, soft piano]
+
+[Interlude: instrumental, warm synth pads]
+
+[Outro: instrumental]
+```
+
+Name the instruments you want inside the labels. Write no words outside the brackets, or they are sung.
+
+`generate.sh`:
+
+```bash
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Generated Music: <name>
+set -euo pipefail
+cd "$(dirname "$0")"
+
+@yue2@ render --lyrics lyrics.txt --seed 1 --out audio.mp3 \
+  --style "instrumental, no vocals, <genre>, <instruments>, <mood>, polished studio recording, 4/4, 90 BPM"
+```
+
+Run it in the background: rendering takes about 0.6 to 0.7 times the length of the audio, usually a few minutes at most.
+
+## The style string
+
+Comma-separated tags in this order: `instrumental, no vocals`, genre, instruments, mood, production, meter, tempo. Keep the meter and `NN BPM` tags: the tool checks the take against them. Name every instrument you want and leave the others out. Describe a reference artist's sound instead of naming them.
+
+For a bed under narration: low-energy or steady, soft instruments, "no heavy drums".
+
+## Length
+
+There is no duration setting. Takes have run from about 90 seconds to over three minutes. Use `Slice:` in the audio plan to take the part the video needs. Add a fade out at the end of the slice.
+
+## After each render
+
+1. Read the check output. `whisper: 0 words` means no vocals. A handful of words or more means the take has singing: change `--seed` and render again. The "lyrics missing or mumbled" note is expected here.
+2. Measure the duration with ffprobe.
+3. You cannot hear audio. Ask the user to listen and report the sections, energy peaks and any vocal sounds.
+4. Write `music.ts` (see [../music.md](../music.md)). Set `source: "local"`, and record the BPM, the seed and the style string in `notes`.
+5. Trigger the approval UX (see [../music.md](../music.md#approval-ux)).
+
+## Iteration on discard
+
+Delete the folder, ask what should change, and change one thing per round: keep the seed to compare style strings, or keep the style and change the seed for a new performance.
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+| Issue | Resolution |
+|---|---|
+| The render fails or times out | The music model and the user's chat model evict each other on the server. Ask the user whether they are chatting, then rerun. |
+| The take has vocals | Change the seed. If it repeats, remove words that suggest singing from the style and labels. |
