+# Local voice generation
+
+## When this is loaded
+
+Flow A step 5: turn `provider_script.md` into a take. The speech models run on the user's own servers. `$TTS_API` and `$STT_API` are already set; there are no keys.
+
+## Generate
+
+Write `generate.sh` in the voiceover folder, run it from the project root, and keep it so the take can be repeated:
+
+```bash
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+node node_modules/videowright/skill/scripts/local-take.mjs "$(dirname "$0")" --seed 1234
+```
+
+The script synthesizes each stretch between `[[pause]]` markers separately, joins them with short silences into `raw.mp3`, and writes word timings to `raw_stt.json`.
+
+| Flag | Default | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| `--seed <n>` | random, printed | The same seed and text give the same audio on `breeze` and `higgs`. Set it in `generate.sh`. |
+| `--model <name>` | `breeze` | See [Voices](../../voiceover.md#voices). |
+| `--voice <id>` | `jeff` | Pair `jeff` with `breeze` or `higgs` only. |
+| `--instruct <text>` | relaxed, conversational | Delivery style, `breeze` only. Change it for the tone from style intake. |
+
+Then continue with [retime.md](../retime.md) from Step 2.
+
+## Takes that need another try
+
+- The check reports a `PROBLEM`, or `apply` finds no natural pause: change `--seed` and run `generate.sh` again.
+- The same line fails every time: reword it, or split it with another `[[pause]]`.
+- A name is mispronounced: spell it the way it sounds in `provider_script.md`.
+- You cannot hear audio. Ask the user to judge voice likeness, pacing and pronunciation.
+- A slow first call or a timeout means the model is loading. Wait and rerun.
